{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/153753-cover-question","id":153753,"title":"Cover Question!?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-30T06:03:14-07:00","id":153753,"title":"Cover Question!?","content":"How exactly does patchworking... work? Soul pact you get the whole person, body and all. Angel-jacking you get a body and a premade cover sort of thing. If you are patchworking, how do you get a new body? When you barter for the body part of the cover, what happens to the person? Or when you start patchworking does a body just appear?<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot; Patchwork<br /> It is possible to build a Cover whole-cloth using the small<br /> pieces of other people\u2019s souls acquired through patch jobs. This<br /> takes some time and the Cover thus created is usually extremely<br /> fragile, but if the character can get it established, it is extremely<br /> difficult to break. Demons that create patchwork Covers find<br /> them to be the most rewarding and comfortable of all Covers \u2014<br /> after all, they are custom made.<br /> System: The demon simply spends Cover experiences<br /> gained from patch jobs (see above) to build a new Cover. This<br /> Cover can wind up being a little disjointed \u2014 the demon takes<br /> a boyfriend from one person, a drug habit from another, and<br /> a job as a ma\u00eetre d\u2019 from a third and has to make it all work<br /> together cohesively \u2014 but once the Cover rating increases<br /> to 5, the Cover solidifies considerably. Patchwork Covers<br /> with ratings of five dots or more are hard to unravel (\u20133 to<br /> all attempts to investigate). Patchwork Covers with ratings of<br /> less than 5, however, are held together precariously (+1 to all<br /> attempts to investigate). &quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T06:28:07-07:00","id":153783,"title":"","content":"Once you get at least 1 dot of Cover bought and switch into that Cover, you now have a body whose appearance is an amalgamation of the people you built your Cover from. A 1 dot Cover is probably going to be pretty recognizable to anyone who knows the people you put it together from, but it is also really thin so that is acceptable. If you want to build a distinct patchwork Cover, you probably want to build a few dots before you start using it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1105-hulsmanm","name":"hulsmanm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T23:25:50-07:00","id":154593,"title":"","content":"Leaving aside bargaining for actual physical characteristics (which I don't know how you'd handle), I feel like hulsmanm's answer is pretty much on the right track. I can only imagine that low rating, single source patchworks resemble an off-brand version of the person you signed on; strong enough features to define as human, certainly, but sort of...generic.<br /> <br /> As you add sources, your features are tweaked and changed here and there by the addition of features from those other sources - not so much as to be unrecognizable, but people who have previously met them might suffer a bit of disconnect, like when you meet someone from highschool several years after the fact and you have to match the person you see with the person you remember. As you raise in rating your features probably shift a little bit and coalesce into looking more like a unique individual than an amalgamation; I'd go ahead and say that when the patchwork hits Cover 5, his features do a few last second changes into creating a unique identity before locking in as the cover's final appearance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T00:27:22-07:00","id":154606,"title":"","content":"I had a player just make a deal for birth sex. They made a major deal, trading birth sex for I believe Resources 5. The victim switched sexes, becoming a non-nondescript male, and everyone's memory sort of adapted to think they had transitioned from female to male.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}